## 1️⃣ WHAT “PHASE B IMPLEMENTED” MEANS (REALISTIC DEFINITION)

For Phase B to be considered *done*, you should have:

### ✅ Chains

* Ethereum / EVM support (ethers or viem)
* Bitcoin support (bitcoinjs-lib)
* Clear separation between chains

### ✅ Assets

* Native coins (ETH, BTC, etc.)
* ERC-20 token handling
* Stablecoin awareness (not auto-conversion yet)

### ✅ Boundaries

* No UI logic
* No private key logging
* Providers injected (Alchemy-ready)

If that matches what you built — **you’re on track**.

---

## 2️⃣ PHASE B VERIFICATION CHECKLIST (DO THIS NOW)

Run through this list **before moving on**:

### 🔍 Code-Level Checks

* [ ] No `console.log(privateKey)`
* [ ] No hardcoded RPC URLs
* [ ] Providers passed as arguments
* [ ] Chain logic does NOT import UI code
* [ ] wallet-core only exposes public interfaces

### 🔍 Functional Checks

* [ ] Can derive ETH address
* [ ] Can derive BTC address
* [ ] Can fetch balance (read-only)
* [ ] Can list supported assets
* [ ] Stablecoins are just *assets*, not logic

If any box is unchecked, fix it **before Phase C**.

---

## 3️⃣ HOW PHASE B SHOULD INTEGRATE WITH WALLET-CORE

This is the **correct dependency direction**:

```
wallet-core  →  chains
     ↑              ↑
 encryption      rpc access
```

### Example (Correct Import Direction)

```ts
// chains/evm.ts
import { deriveEthereumAccount } from "wallet-core";
```

❌ NEVER do this:

```ts
// wallet-core importing chains ❌
import { getEthBalance } from "../chains/evm";
```

Wallet-core must remain **chain-agnostic**.

